WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.029 --> 00:00:02.130
- What makes a superhero a superhero?

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:03.088
That's a hard question.

00:00:03.088 --> 00:00:05.182
- Superheros are people
who look out for others.

00:00:05.182 --> 00:00:06.831
- The fact that they never give up,

00:00:06.831 --> 00:00:08.526
always just in favor of justice.

00:00:08.526 --> 00:00:10.570
- Owning up to things
that you're afraid of?

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.351
- I think heroes can come
in all shapes and forms

00:00:12.351 --> 00:00:14.285
and it's really about owning who you are,

00:00:14.285 --> 00:00:16.202
standing up for what you believe in.

00:00:16.202 --> 00:00:18.785
(upbeat music)

00:00:21.047 --> 00:00:23.960
- Today we are recreating
iconic superhero moments.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.425
We specifically are going
to be doing the famous

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:28.718
upside-down kiss between
Peter Parker and Mary Jane.

00:00:28.718 --> 00:00:30.268
- I honestly think it's
one of the most iconic

00:00:30.268 --> 00:00:31.365
superhero scenes of all time.

00:00:31.365 --> 00:00:33.656
- Probably one of the most
iconic kisses in movie history.

00:00:33.656 --> 00:00:35.647
- Today I'm going to be recreating

00:00:35.647 --> 00:00:37.847
the iconic Superman photo.

00:00:37.847 --> 00:00:41.548
Superman has this very iconic,
classic, all American look.

00:00:41.548 --> 00:00:44.277
I'm excited to kind of put a flip on it.

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.508
- The image that we are recreating today

00:00:46.508 --> 00:00:48.823
is Wolverine coming out of the tank,

00:00:48.823 --> 00:00:50.476
and just so fucking angry.

00:00:50.476 --> 00:00:52.811
I am so excited to do this piece because

00:00:52.811 --> 00:00:56.188
as a trans-person, it
is exactly how I felt

00:00:56.188 --> 00:01:00.481
when I was able to be myself,
and to just be 100% happy

00:01:00.481 --> 00:01:02.911
in my own fucking body and no
one gets to take that from me.

00:01:02.911 --> 00:01:04.497
- All right, let's take these photos.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.230
- One, two, three.

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:08.469
Your hand is up, not like this.

00:01:08.469 --> 00:01:09.302
- Aaaaaahhhhhhhh!

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.318
- [Macey] Yeah, better.

00:01:10.318 --> 00:01:12.454
- So I'm getting ready to recreate this

00:01:12.454 --> 00:01:14.328
Christopher Reeves Superman photo.

00:01:14.328 --> 00:01:16.646
It's in Superman three,
right after Superman fights

00:01:16.646 --> 00:01:17.752
Negative Superman.

00:01:17.752 --> 00:01:20.485
- So we're filming this in a studio.

00:01:20.485 --> 00:01:23.186
We're going to put in the
background after the fact.

00:01:23.186 --> 00:01:25.346
- I'm wearing this suit
and it has this, like,

00:01:25.346 --> 00:01:28.786
beige skin, so it's
like built in whiteness.

00:01:28.786 --> 00:01:30.714
Unfortunately, you get
used to the fact that

00:01:30.714 --> 00:01:32.693
the world is made for white people.

00:01:32.693 --> 00:01:34.770
And they don't often consider that

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.232
some people are not this shade.

00:01:36.232 --> 00:01:38.390
I feel like seeing Superman as a black man

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:40.738
is important to put that image out there

00:01:40.738 --> 00:01:42.362
that anybody can be Superman.

00:01:42.362 --> 00:01:45.249
And Superman represents so
many different types of people.

00:01:45.249 --> 00:01:46.642
- [Macey] One, two, three.

00:01:46.642 --> 00:01:47.475
- Cool!

00:01:47.475 --> 00:01:48.308
- Yeah.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:49.849
- Ooh, I really like that one.

00:01:49.849 --> 00:01:50.783
(synthesizer music)

00:01:50.783 --> 00:01:53.958
- So we're having a very
serious issue right now.

00:01:53.958 --> 00:01:55.234
It turns out that the

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:56.399
- I don't think so. (laughing)

00:01:56.399 --> 00:01:58.136
Spider-man costume we got,

00:01:58.136 --> 00:02:00.535
the mask is attached

00:02:00.535 --> 00:02:01.927
to the body.

00:02:01.927 --> 00:02:04.416
So we can't actually do the lifting up

00:02:04.416 --> 00:02:06.617
that we need for the photo.

00:02:06.617 --> 00:02:08.400
- Yeah, I think it works, right?

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.328
- Originally I thought that I was actually

00:02:10.328 --> 00:02:12.795
gonna be upside-down,
but we're going to get

00:02:12.795 --> 00:02:15.693
two separate images of us kissing,

00:02:15.693 --> 00:02:18.122
and then in photo shop combine them.

00:02:18.122 --> 00:02:19.875
(laughing)

00:02:19.875 --> 00:02:21.997
- [Voiceover] This looks a lot
more romantic in the movie.

00:02:21.997 --> 00:02:24.667
- [Macey] Open your
mouth a little bit, Yeah.

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:26.497
- I think Hollywood
gets in this rut of just

00:02:26.497 --> 00:02:28.581
churning out the same thing
over and over and over again.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:31.048
Something as simple as
changing the gender,

00:02:31.048 --> 00:02:33.044
the sexuality, or the
race of your character

00:02:33.044 --> 00:02:34.976
can lead you to create different stories.

00:02:34.976 --> 00:02:35.934
And that's what people want.

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:37.207
- It looked good.

00:02:37.207 --> 00:02:38.193
- All right. We did it.

00:02:38.193 --> 00:02:39.026
- Great job.
- U got it?

00:02:39.026 --> 00:02:39.859
- Yeah.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.050
- All these movies are
about overcoming adversity.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.532
It's about being shunned
by society and having to

00:02:43.532 --> 00:02:45.790
be yourself regardless
of what people think.

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:47.936
And that is all what queer people

00:02:47.936 --> 00:02:49.548
have to go through every single day.

00:02:49.548 --> 00:02:51.078
- One, two, three. Yep.

00:02:51.078 --> 00:02:52.983
- My favorite superhero is Wolverine.

00:02:52.983 --> 00:02:55.136
As a trans-person, I
wanted to be something

00:02:55.136 --> 00:02:56.942
just as masculine as Wolverine.

00:02:56.942 --> 00:02:58.752
- They shouldn't go lower than,

00:02:58.752 --> 00:03:00.538
like a little bit past your armpit.

00:03:00.538 --> 00:03:01.371
- I feel pretty good.

00:03:01.371 --> 00:03:03.569
I mean, it's cool that
these are real metal claws.

00:03:03.569 --> 00:03:04.461
I wasn't expecting that.

00:03:04.461 --> 00:03:05.294
They're hella heavy.

00:03:05.294 --> 00:03:06.565
Something that's really important to me is

00:03:06.565 --> 00:03:08.823
every time that I see
Wolverine wearing his dogtags,

00:03:08.823 --> 00:03:10.740
reminds me of my struggles in the military

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:11.819
as a trans-person.

00:03:11.819 --> 00:03:13.876
It felt really cool seeing
the pictures afterwards.

00:03:13.876 --> 00:03:17.034
I can't wait to see
what the end result is.

00:03:17.034 --> 00:03:18.702
(synthesizer music)

00:03:18.702 --> 00:03:21.037
The shoot was pretty freaking awesome.

00:03:21.037 --> 00:03:22.486
Growing up, I never thought I would

00:03:22.486 --> 00:03:23.902
do a photo shoot of Wolverine.

00:03:23.902 --> 00:03:25.664
It's like, for Halloween,
I always wanted that

00:03:25.664 --> 00:03:28.457
Wolverine costume but I knew
that I could never have it.

00:03:28.457 --> 00:03:30.875
If there was a lot more
diversity in superhero movies

00:03:30.875 --> 00:03:32.865
I would have had a different childhood.

00:03:32.865 --> 00:03:35.643
I think that I wouldn't
have struggled so much

00:03:35.643 --> 00:03:37.582
with myself and my identity.

00:03:37.582 --> 00:03:40.820
I'm keeping these, by the way. (laughing)

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.830
- It is really cool to
be wearing this suit

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:46.357
and actually looking in the
mirror and seeing myself

00:03:46.357 --> 00:03:47.706
looking like Spider-man.

00:03:47.706 --> 00:03:51.034
If someone asked me,
"What makes Spider-man,

00:03:51.034 --> 00:03:53.212
Spider-man," I'd think his intelligence.

00:03:53.212 --> 00:03:55.643
I'd think his courage,
his passion, his love.

00:03:55.643 --> 00:03:58.332
I don't think his whiteness
or his straightness.

00:03:58.332 --> 00:04:00.386
I don't think that's
essential to who he is.

00:04:00.386 --> 00:04:02.799
- Through talking about
the idea of Superman

00:04:02.799 --> 00:04:05.458
and kind of how he represents this

00:04:05.458 --> 00:04:07.742
ideal, all-American citizen.

00:04:07.742 --> 00:04:09.740
And then kind of relating that to how,

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:12.324
in today's terms, anyone
can be that ideal citizen.

00:04:12.324 --> 00:04:13.716
Who cares if he's a gay black man?

00:04:13.716 --> 00:04:15.442
If you're burning in a
building, Superman is still

00:04:15.442 --> 00:04:17.234
gonna swoop in and save the day.

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:18.180
Go be a hero.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:19.310
You don't have to wear a cape.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:22.579
Sometimes you can just
wear drag. (laughing)

00:04:22.579 --> 00:04:24.409
- People want to see themselves in movies.

00:04:24.409 --> 00:04:26.162
They want to see themselves as heroes.

00:04:26.162 --> 00:04:28.635
So let's make more of
an effort to represent

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:29.928
more people in society.

00:04:29.928 --> 00:04:31.596
So if a little gay kid is growing up,

00:04:31.596 --> 00:04:33.372
they can see themselves represented.

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:36.805
And you know, they can aspire
to be a hero themselves.

00:04:36.805 --> 00:04:37.638
Tss. Tss.

00:04:37.638 --> 00:04:38.517
(one clap)

00:04:38.517 --> 00:04:39.783
- [Director] Cut.

00:04:39.783 --> 00:04:42.950
(upbeat heroic music)

